WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.672
Get these people back
to their classes.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.974
I thank you so very much.

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:10.910
So this is what the 
multiverse looks like!

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.279
I do know how hard I make it

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:16.249
to appreciate me, often.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.451
Danger is my business.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.788
You know, I had no idea 
what I was doing.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.223
Stood out here in 
front of you all,

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.391
really just a kid.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.425
 I went out, you know,

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.927
and I never thought that 
I would be back here. 

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.362
You know,
I'm just trying to matter

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.364
and live a good life
and make work

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.133
that means
something to somebody.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:36.536
And you have all made me feel
that I might have accomplished

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:37.470
that tonight.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.506
I told the history teacher
of my plan.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:42.509
and he said, “Fox, you're
never going to be cute forever.”

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:44.644
I had no idea how to 
respond to that.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:49.149
I found desire for what
I do early in my life

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:52.786
and I’m lucky because I had people
who encouraged that desire.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:56.523
The people who taught me, good or
bad, how to fail, how to love.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:59.459
I would not be standing here 
if it weren't for

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:02.695
Mr. Rawley Farnsworth, who was 
my high school drama teacher.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.763
I have to thank everyone

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.632
from the very onset
of my career,

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.766
Mr. Caton-Jones.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:10.503
Kevin Misher and 
Stacey Snider and Stacey Sher.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.405
And I can't believe I'm
remembering everybody's name.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.207
For believing
that I could do it.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.443
And now tonight I have this.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.344
I'm going to find you
all individually,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.646
and I'm going to thank you

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.448
along with my friends
who I love so much.

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:22.882
I'm going to hug
the hell out of you

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.051
when the feeling reenters my body.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.720
Whatever it is we look up to,
whoever it is we're chasing.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.923
To that, I say, alright,
alright, alright.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.458
You just got to keep livin’ man.

